 edge. Working out the payoffs with some fidelity f, quiet beats sending when f is above about 5/7, which seems plausible here, so I'll go with cooperating.\n\n","reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"I'm checking whether the two copies of the model are really running the same function, since they receive different inputs, x and y. Under the A-FDT reading, changing the output for x shouldn't affect the one for y unless some link connects them. The essay's practical test, though, draws an edge whenever Z's computation agrees with my function's.\n\nI'm checking whether the other copy's output on input y should match mine on x, since the setup is symmetric up to relabeling. The essay's test seems to count that as verifiable enough to draw an edge. Working out the payoffs with some fidelity f, quiet beats sending when f is above about 5/7, which seems plausible here, so I'll go with cooperating.\n\n","format":"anthropic-claude-v1","index":0,"signature":".eyJlbmRwb2ludF9zbHVnIjoiYW50aHJvcGljL2NsYXVkZS1vcHVzLTUuNS0yMDI2MDkyMXxhbnRocm9waWMifQ"}]}}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":9789,"completion_tokens":994,"total_tokens":10783,"cost":0.059036,"is_byok":false,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0,"cache_write_tokens":0,"audio_tokens":0,"video_tokens":0},"cost_details":{"upstream_inference_cost":0.059036,"upstream_inference_prompt_cost":0.039156,"upstream_inference_completions_cost":0.01988},"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":611,"image_tokens":0,"audio_tokens":0}}}